A12-do-i-need-dynamodb-for-locks.with-skill:
No — per knowledge card aws-s3-native-state-locking, since AWS provider 5.55 / Terraform 1.10 (June 2024) the s3 backend supports `use_lockfile = true` for native state locking. A DynamoDB table is no longer required.
```hcl
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket       = "my-tf-state"
    key          = "prod/terraform.tfstate"
    region       = "us-east-1"
    encrypt      = true
    use_lockfile = true
  }
}
```
